    "Sufficient evidence has been submitted to demonstrate, on the balance of probabilities, that the property has been in continuous use as a large House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) falling within the Sui Generis use class for a period exceeding 10 years prior to the date of the application. The submitted documentation, including tenancy agreements, landlord statements, utility and council tax records, and evidence of ongoing management and maintenance, supports the conclusion that the use is lawful and immune from enforcement action under Section 171B(3) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended)."
